Package: bonsaiR
Type: Package
Title: R Wrapper for the Bonsai Single-Cell Tree Reconstruction Method
Version: 0.1.0
Author: person("Your", "Name", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Maintainer: Your Name <you@example.com>
Description: Provides an R interface, via reticulate and system calls, to the
    Python/C++ Bonsai tool stack (Sanity, cellstates, Bonsai) for
    reconstructing maximum-likelihood tree representations of single-cell
    RNA-seq data starting from Seurat objects. Computationally heavy steps
    (Sanity, cellstates, and the core Bonsai tree search) are run as external
    CLI processes -- optionally under local MPI parallelization -- rather
    than in-process, since Bonsai's tree search is designed around
    multi-process MPI execution which is not achievable through an embedded
    reticulate interpreter. Lightweight, single-process downstream analyses
    (e.g. marker gene detection) are called directly via reticulate.
